<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ninhursag</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ninhursag was a Sumerian mother goddess associated with birth, fertility and the mountains. She was worshipped at Kesh and at Adab, whose main temple, the E-sar, was hers, and Sumerian kings described themselves as nourished by her milk. In the myth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enki">Enki</a> and Ninhursag, set in the pure land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilmun">Dilmun</a>, she curses the god Enki and then heals him.</p></div>
